WEBVTT

00:01:30.540 --> 00:01:34.500
<b>Presence</b>

00:06:25.170 --> 00:06:28.460
<b>Presence, Continued</b>

00:08:33.460 --> 00:08:35.790
Good morning, Yukari-chan!

00:08:37.830 --> 00:08:40.420
What've you been doing back there, anyways?

00:08:40.420 --> 00:08:43.040
Nothing...

00:08:43.040 --> 00:08:44.250
Let's walk together!

00:08:44.420 --> 00:08:46.630
Uh... sure.

00:08:47.380 --> 00:08:52.460
I thought I saw Sanae-chan walking ahead of me, too.
Have you seen her?

00:08:52.460 --> 00:08:54.630
Nope. I haven't.

00:08:57.580 --> 00:09:00.960
<b>Desk Check</b>

00:08:58.670 --> 00:09:00.500
Desk Check.

00:09:03.380 --> 00:09:07.080
I just remembered,
I think we have a desk check later today.

00:09:07.380 --> 00:09:09.710
Oh yeah? I didn't realize.

00:09:10.040 --> 00:09:12.460
Really? You don't seem worried.

00:09:12.460 --> 00:09:14.670
Well, I don't have anything that would get me in trouble.

00:09:15.000 --> 00:09:16.080
Are you sure?

00:09:17.670 --> 00:09:20.880
Uh, you're making me start to lose confidence...

00:09:21.040 --> 00:09:25.040
It's possible that I may have brought some
manga or a game from home without thinking.

00:09:25.960 --> 00:09:29.710
Thanks, now I'm getting freaked out and it's all your fault.

00:09:31.460 --> 00:09:33.920
Okay. Then why don't we do a practice run?

00:09:33.920 --> 00:09:35.210
Before the real thing.

00:09:35.380 --> 00:09:37.170
What's the point of that?

00:09:37.170 --> 00:09:40.500
If we check your desk now,
then you don't have to panic later.

00:09:43.290 --> 00:09:44.880
Okay. I'll check everything from your desk.

00:09:51.670 --> 00:09:54.080
This is just making me even more nervous...

00:09:54.790 --> 00:09:57.130
E-everything's cool, right?

00:09:57.790 --> 00:09:59.130
Nishikata-kun!

00:09:59.580 --> 00:10:01.880
You must address your teachers with proper respect!

00:10:01.880 --> 00:10:03.960
She's totally hamming this up.

00:10:04.750 --> 00:10:05.540
Yes, ma'am.

00:10:05.540 --> 00:10:06.460
That's more like it.

00:10:09.630 --> 00:10:11.380
AH HAH! YOU'RE BUSTED!

00:10:11.460 --> 00:10:13.630
Oh crap! Did she find something bad?!

00:10:13.630 --> 00:10:15.460
I'm doomed!

00:10:17.000 --> 00:10:19.830
Never mind. It was just your English textbook.

00:10:21.290 --> 00:10:22.580
Did I scare you?

00:10:22.960 --> 00:10:26.250
N-not even a little. It's cool.

00:10:29.630 --> 00:10:31.750
You didn't scare me, ma'am.

00:10:32.630 --> 00:10:33.880
Very good.

00:10:34.880 --> 00:10:36.790
Okay. Now it's my turn.

00:10:37.130 --> 00:10:38.880
Sure. Fine with me.

00:10:38.960 --> 00:10:39.960
<b>Math</b>

00:10:41.630 --> 00:10:43.670
Please go ahead, sir!

00:10:43.920 --> 00:10:44.710
Splendid.

00:10:45.580 --> 00:10:47.750
I'm gonna give Takagi-san the scare of her life!

00:10:50.710 --> 00:10:54.250
"Splendid"? Your impression of an adult sure is funny.

00:10:55.830 --> 00:10:57.960
A-address your teachers with respect!

00:10:58.080 --> 00:10:59.290
Yes, sir.

00:10:59.540 --> 00:11:03.170
Darn you, Takagi-san!
I'm supposed to have the upper hand right now!

00:11:08.750 --> 00:11:11.080
She looks like she doesn't have a care in the world.

00:11:11.330 --> 00:11:14.460
I'm betting that means there's nothing in
her desk that could get in her in trouble.

00:11:15.330 --> 00:11:17.250
Fine. Then I'll just have to fake it!

00:11:18.380 --> 00:11:21.710
Wait. Is it me or is there something
hidden in her gym clothes?

00:11:22.210 --> 00:11:23.710
Could it be...?

00:11:24.080 --> 00:11:26.920
She must be trying to bluff me with that smile!

00:11:27.130 --> 00:11:28.630
Is something the matter, sir?

00:11:29.040 --> 00:11:31.170
I'll pressure her into confessing!

00:11:31.880 --> 00:11:34.920
Those gym clothes...
it sure looks like you're hiding something under them.

00:11:35.130 --> 00:11:36.500
Then feel free to check them out.

00:11:37.710 --> 00:11:39.880
Please. Go right ahead, sir.

00:11:45.670 --> 00:11:48.420
What? Is there a problem?

00:11:48.540 --> 00:11:51.460
You know I'm way too embarrassed to
even try touching your gym clothes!

00:11:51.750 --> 00:11:52.670
Five...

00:11:53.460 --> 00:11:53.960
Four...

00:11:54.290 --> 00:11:54.880
W-w-w-wait!

00:11:54.880 --> 00:11:55.420
Three...
W-w-w-wait!<b></b>

00:11:55.420 --> 00:11:56.330
W-w-w-wait!

00:11:56.380 --> 00:11:57.170
Two...

00:11:57.960 --> 00:11:58.710
One...

00:11:59.710 --> 00:12:00.500
Zero!

00:12:01.080 --> 00:12:02.210
Time's up.

00:12:02.420 --> 00:12:04.250
Why is Takagi-san making up all these rules?!

00:12:04.250 --> 00:12:07.540
I'm supposed to be the teacher here!
But she's too imposing!

00:12:07.750 --> 00:12:10.420
Well, you can relax,
because there is no desk check today.

00:12:10.420 --> 00:12:11.000
Huh?!

00:12:11.130 --> 00:12:13.000
I just "thought" we might have one.

00:12:15.040 --> 00:12:17.330
You just took me for a ride...

00:12:17.630 --> 00:12:18.790
Oh, right.

00:12:21.710 --> 00:12:23.670
Here. Thanks for lending me this.

00:12:22.290 --> 00:12:23.710
<b>Psychic Red</b>

00:12:23.790 --> 00:12:25.000
I knew it!

00:12:26.460 --> 00:12:29.290
You're too easy, Nishikata-sensei.

00:12:35.460 --> 00:12:38.420
Feel free to do a surprise desk check on me anytime.

00:12:39.250 --> 00:12:41.250
Curse you, Takagi-san!

00:12:42.420 --> 00:12:43.670
Library duty.

00:12:42.420 --> 00:12:44.880
<b>Library Duty</b>

00:12:43.670 --> 00:12:44.790
Okay.

00:12:44.920 --> 00:12:46.830
On culture fest duty we have...

00:12:46.920 --> 00:12:48.580
Kimura and Tsukimoto.

00:12:49.080 --> 00:12:50.790
And on library duty...

00:12:51.080 --> 00:12:55.000
<b>Library</b>

00:12:51.130 --> 00:12:53.630
Do you see this card that's in the back of each book?

00:12:53.830 --> 00:12:57.790
Just take that out and write the
student's name and the date.

00:12:55.040 --> 00:12:59.210
<b>Inner Emptiness</b>

00:12:55.040 --> 00:12:59.210
<b>Muroi Masamichi</b>

00:12:57.790 --> 00:12:59.960
Then you keep the card here.

00:13:00.040 --> 00:13:04.000
And when they return the book,
write the date and place it back into the book.

00:13:04.380 --> 00:13:05.500
That's about it.

00:13:05.500 --> 00:13:06.670
Pretty easy, right?

00:13:06.920 --> 00:13:12.830
<b>Library</b>

00:13:07.080 --> 00:13:07.960
All right.

00:13:08.210 --> 00:13:11.750
I don't think many students will come,
so try to stay focused.

00:13:15.290 --> 00:13:18.670
Crap, we have to waste our lunch
break on this once a week now.

00:13:18.880 --> 00:13:22.250
What's the problem?
We can read novels to pass the time.

00:13:22.380 --> 00:13:24.460
Aw man, novels?

00:13:24.460 --> 00:13:26.380
They're fun to read, trust me.

00:13:26.380 --> 00:13:28.420
So what, you read often or something?

00:13:28.420 --> 00:13:31.040
I'd say I split my time evenly between manga and novels.

00:13:31.330 --> 00:13:33.420
You don't seem like you read much at all, though.

00:13:34.080 --> 00:13:37.130
Well, I'll have you know that I do... on occasion.

00:13:39.080 --> 00:13:41.420
Let's go pick out some books. We've got nothing else to do.

00:13:47.290 --> 00:13:48.880
A book, huh?

00:13:53.580 --> 00:13:56.210
Gotta say, they all seem pretty boring to me...

00:13:57.080 --> 00:13:59.290
But maybe I can find something.

00:14:00.460 --> 00:14:02.290
<b>AN</b>

00:14:00.460 --> 00:14:02.290
<b>ILLUSTRATED</b>

00:14:00.460 --> 00:14:02.290
<b>GUIDE TO</b>

00:14:00.460 --> 00:14:02.290
<b>DINOSAURS</b>

00:14:04.330 --> 00:14:06.210
Dinosaurs!

00:14:07.000 --> 00:14:09.170
Sweet! I love picture books!

00:14:09.380 --> 00:14:11.080
Did you find something good?

00:14:11.790 --> 00:14:13.500
No, not really.

00:14:14.500 --> 00:14:18.170
That was close!
She'd totally call me a baby for reading picture books!

00:14:18.960 --> 00:14:21.130
Hey, I have an idea.

00:14:21.130 --> 00:14:24.210
Let's pick out a book for each other.
Then we'll read them together, okay?

00:14:24.330 --> 00:14:26.460
Huh? Okay, sure.

00:14:26.460 --> 00:14:27.420
No take-backsies!

00:14:39.580 --> 00:14:40.830
<b>Bryan</b>

00:14:39.580 --> 00:14:40.830
<b>By Tomoko Minakami</b>

00:14:42.130 --> 00:14:44.210
I've never read this one before.

00:14:44.210 --> 00:14:45.420
I wonder what it's about?

00:14:45.420 --> 00:14:48.710
I don't know anything about it, I just went with my gut.

00:14:51.670 --> 00:14:53.420
The illustrated guide to Dinosaurs?!

00:14:54.210 --> 00:14:56.750
You looked like you were really enjoying it.

00:14:57.880 --> 00:14:59.290
She knew the whole time...

00:15:01.170 --> 00:15:02.790
<b>Lexovisaurus</b>

00:15:01.170 --> 00:15:02.790
<b>Arrhinoceratops</b>

00:15:01.170 --> 00:15:02.790
<b>Gorgosaurus</b>

00:15:12.500 --> 00:15:16.000
Takagi-san... sure looks cute when she reads a book.

00:15:18.290 --> 00:15:19.710
Were you just looking at me?

00:15:20.000 --> 00:15:21.960
No, I wasn't looking anywhere.

00:15:23.790 --> 00:15:25.080
Ah! I get it.

00:15:25.380 --> 00:15:27.250
Since we're all alone right now,

00:15:27.250 --> 00:15:30.540
you were thinking about getting your
revenge by teasing me back somehow.

00:15:32.540 --> 00:15:35.330
W-well, I guess you could say it was something like that...

00:15:39.380 --> 00:15:40.460
I love you.

00:15:42.420 --> 00:15:43.540
Huh?

00:15:44.830 --> 00:15:46.540
Uh, say what now?

00:15:46.540 --> 00:15:50.290
As those words came from Yaotome's lips,
Tanaka responded by dropping his drink in shock.

00:15:50.290 --> 00:15:51.500
Out in the field,

00:15:51.500 --> 00:15:53.210
She was reading aloud...
the shouts of the baseball club members echoed...<b></b>

00:15:55.000 --> 00:15:56.380
Something wrong?

00:15:56.670 --> 00:15:59.420
Darn you, Takagi-san!

00:16:00.080 --> 00:16:02.500
<b>Library</b>

00:16:02.580 --> 00:16:05.290
Nobody came to borrow a book today.

00:16:05.290 --> 00:16:07.580
I hope next week is the same.

00:16:09.460 --> 00:16:10.670
Same here.

00:16:11.670 --> 00:16:14.830
You should read a novel next week, too, Nishikata.

00:16:16.210 --> 00:16:18.710
Well, is there anything that you'd recommend?

00:16:20.500 --> 00:16:22.040
Good question.

00:16:22.290 --> 00:16:26.000
I'd recommend everything in the library,
other than the book you picked out today.

00:16:26.130 --> 00:16:26.920
Huh?!

00:16:26.920 --> 00:16:28.750
Was it really that horrible of a story?!

00:16:28.750 --> 00:16:29.580
No.

00:16:29.580 --> 00:16:30.880
I enjoyed it, actually.

00:16:31.250 --> 00:16:33.460
I just wouldn't recommend it to you.

00:16:33.750 --> 00:16:35.210
How does that work?

00:16:35.920 --> 00:16:38.830
Because then you'd find out
that line wasn't from the book...

00:16:39.580 --> 00:16:41.080
Huh? Did you say something?

00:16:41.080 --> 00:16:42.380
Nothing at all.

00:16:42.540 --> 00:16:44.920
What? C'mon, I know you said something!

00:16:45.420 --> 00:16:47.130
Takagi-san! What was it?

00:16:47.420 --> 00:16:50.880
<b>Sunset</b>

00:16:48.630 --> 00:16:50.000
Sunset.

00:16:55.380 --> 00:16:56.920
Nishikata!

00:16:58.460 --> 00:17:00.580
Hey, Takagi-san! What're you doing?

00:17:00.580 --> 00:17:01.710
Running errands!

00:17:01.710 --> 00:17:02.750
What about you?

00:17:02.960 --> 00:17:04.380
Going for a jog.

00:17:04.380 --> 00:17:05.460
Wow!

00:17:05.790 --> 00:17:07.080
Do you go for a jog every day?

00:17:07.080 --> 00:17:09.170
No. Just sometimes.

00:17:09.380 --> 00:17:13.750
Jogging kind of became a habit of mine,
after I started doing it to practice for the marathon.

00:17:13.830 --> 00:17:16.170
Oh? I didn't even know you trained for that.

00:17:16.710 --> 00:17:18.420
And yet you still lost to me!

00:17:16.710 --> 00:17:18.290
<b>Girls Turn</b>

00:17:16.710 --> 00:17:18.290
<b>Back Here</b>

00:17:19.500 --> 00:17:20.710
Darn her.

00:17:21.460 --> 00:17:23.130
I'm gonna win next time.

00:17:23.830 --> 00:17:25.170
I'd love to see that.

00:17:25.420 --> 00:17:27.290
So, how far do you go?

00:17:27.750 --> 00:17:30.630
Well, it's not really a set thing.

00:17:30.630 --> 00:17:32.670
I just kind of quit when I get tired.

00:17:32.670 --> 00:17:34.880
Y'know, one time I went as far as the
beach on the other side of town!

00:17:34.960 --> 00:17:37.290
That far? Wow!

00:17:37.420 --> 00:17:41.170
Whoa! Takagi-san is actually impressed by me for once!

00:17:41.170 --> 00:17:42.580
This is a good chance...

00:17:42.830 --> 00:17:43.790
I'm not sure I believe you.

00:17:43.790 --> 00:17:45.250
But I'm telling the truth!

00:17:45.250 --> 00:17:47.630
That's pretty far away though.

00:17:47.830 --> 00:17:49.210
It sounds like you're lying.

00:17:49.210 --> 00:17:51.460
I'm serious! It happened!

00:17:53.250 --> 00:17:55.670
Okay. Well, good luck.

00:17:56.250 --> 00:17:57.670
Bye bye!

00:17:58.080 --> 00:18:00.080
She clearly doesn't believe me!

00:18:00.080 --> 00:18:05.210
Fine! I'll run all the way there right now
and prove it to her with a picture!

00:18:06.670 --> 00:18:10.630
Get ready, Takagi-san! Cuz I'm gonna blow you away!

00:18:13.830 --> 00:18:15.420
This is killing me...

00:18:25.960 --> 00:18:29.750
I was already thinking about going
home when I ran into her,

00:18:29.750 --> 00:18:31.420
so my stamina is shot...

00:18:35.290 --> 00:18:36.750
I'm gonna die...

00:18:37.830 --> 00:18:39.380
I better call it quits.

00:18:42.080 --> 00:18:44.170
No! I have to do this!

00:18:44.380 --> 00:18:45.920
If I make to the beach...

00:18:46.500 --> 00:18:48.420
Seriously? That's amazing, Nishikata!

00:18:48.420 --> 00:18:49.710
I'll never tease you again!

00:18:49.710 --> 00:18:51.080
That's what'll happen!

00:18:55.000 --> 00:18:58.500
Just you wait! Takagi-san!

00:19:04.130 --> 00:19:05.630
I made it...

00:19:16.460 --> 00:19:18.830
I feel so accomplished right now.

00:19:19.290 --> 00:19:19.830
Wait!

00:19:19.830 --> 00:19:23.210
That's not what's important!
I have to send a picture to Takagi-san!

00:19:23.750 --> 00:19:25.580
Okay. Done.

00:19:24.000 --> 00:19:25.130
<b>TAKAGI-SAN</b>

00:19:24.000 --> 00:19:25.130
<b>Why?!</b>

00:19:24.000 --> 00:19:25.130
<b>Today</b>

00:19:24.000 --> 00:19:25.130
<b>I made it to the beach.</b>

00:19:27.250 --> 00:19:30.000
In your face, Takagi-san! Bow before my awesomeness!

00:19:30.790 --> 00:19:33.210
<b>The sunset looks so pretty.</b>

00:19:30.790 --> 00:19:33.210
<b>Thank you.</b>

00:19:37.210 --> 00:19:39.920
Darn it! That's not what matters! Look at where I am!

00:19:39.920 --> 00:19:43.580
I didn't send you that picture for you
to admire the sunset, Takagi-san!

00:19:43.580 --> 00:19:44.420
You didn't?

00:19:50.130 --> 00:19:52.420
Takagi-san! What're you doing out here?!

00:19:54.130 --> 00:19:56.210
Your reactions are always so amusing.

00:19:56.630 --> 00:20:00.330
It was worth racing down here on
my bike after I finished my errands.

00:20:00.920 --> 00:20:01.830
Here.

00:20:06.830 --> 00:20:08.040
Thanks...

00:20:19.880 --> 00:20:23.670
I figured you'd go all the way to
the beach to prove it to me.

00:20:23.920 --> 00:20:25.330
And here you are!

00:20:26.580 --> 00:20:28.830
I fell for her tricks again!

00:20:30.130 --> 00:20:31.880
But I'm flattered.

00:20:31.880 --> 00:20:37.580
I mean, you ran your butt off all the way here just
to send me that picture of the sunset, didn't you?

00:20:37.580 --> 00:20:41.250
Well, sure, but you're kind of missing the point...

00:20:42.130 --> 00:20:43.290
Red as a tomato.

00:20:43.290 --> 00:20:43.920
No...

00:20:45.380 --> 00:20:46.040
I'm-!

00:20:46.040 --> 00:20:47.000
The sunset, that is.

00:20:49.790 --> 00:20:50.710
Forget it.

00:20:51.330 --> 00:20:53.670
Well, you're even redder than that right now!

00:20:54.330 --> 00:20:57.920
Crap! All I wanted was to impress her!

00:20:57.920 --> 00:20:59.920
I worked so hard to make that happen, yet...!

00:21:01.540 --> 00:21:04.630
It was so worth it to chase after you!

00:21:08.750 --> 00:21:10.330
For this chance to...

00:21:10.960 --> 00:21:12.170
Watch the sunset together.

00:21:15.790 --> 00:21:17.290
It's so pretty.

00:21:25.250 --> 00:21:26.960
As if! She's lying!

00:21:26.960 --> 00:21:29.960
I know she's only here to tease me! I won't fall for it!

00:21:30.670 --> 00:21:31.710
Darn it!

00:21:31.710 --> 00:21:35.080
I'm such an idiot for letting myself get excited like that.

00:21:37.880 --> 00:21:40.630
I've gotta hand it to you, it is impressive.

00:21:40.960 --> 00:21:42.750
You really did run all the way to the beach.

00:21:54.170 --> 00:21:56.080
Whatever. It was nothing.

00:21:56.500 --> 00:21:59.380
Don't pretend.
That compliment just put a smirk on your face.

00:21:59.460 --> 00:22:00.880
I ain't smirking!

00:22:00.880 --> 00:22:03.210
I accomplished my goal, but...
Well, it looks like a smirk to me.<b></b>

00:22:03.210 --> 00:22:03.830
Trust me, it's not!

00:22:03.830 --> 00:22:04.500
it doesn't feel like I won against her in the slightest.
Trust me, it's not!<b></b>

00:22:04.500 --> 00:22:06.170
it doesn't feel like I won against her in the slightest.
That's not convincing. I mean, your face is red.<b></b>

00:22:06.170 --> 00:22:06.630
That's not convincing. I mean, your face is red.

00:22:06.630 --> 00:22:08.460
T-that's just your imagination!
